  "problem": {
    "statement": "### Description\n\n### Description\nWhen configuring an OAuth2 Authentication Service through the Gitea web interface, the suggested Redirect/Callback URL fails to properly encode apostrophes in the Authentication Name field.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n- Navigate to Site Administration \u2192 Authentication Sources\n- Add a new OAuth2 authentication source\n- Enter an Authentication Name containing an apostrophe (e.g., LiBER's Microsoft Entra)\n- Observe the auto-generated Redirect/Callback URL\n\n### Expected Behavior\nThe apostrophe character ' should be percent-encoded as %27 in the suggested Redirect/Callback URL according to RFC 3986.\nExample: https://gitea.internal.liberbattery.it/user/oauth2/LiBER%27s%20Microsoft%20Entra/callback\n\n### Actual Behavior\nThe apostrophe remains unencoded in the suggested URL.\nExample: https://gitea.internal.liberbattery.it/user/oauth2/LiBER's%20Microsoft%20Entra/callback\n\n### Impact\nThis creates an invalid URL that will cause OAuth2 callback failures when the authentication provider attempts to redirect back to Gitea. You have to change the Redirect URL manually\n\n### Screenshots\n\n<img width=\"993\" height=\"360\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/58bc0e72-796a-42fb-aff7-94175ff4c477\" />\n\n### Gitea Version\n\n1.25.3 built with GNU Make 4.4.1, go1.25.5 : bindata, timetzdata, sqlite, sqlite_unlock_notify\n\n### Can you reproduce the bug on the Gitea demo site?\n\nNo\n\n### Operating System\n\n_No response_\n\n### Browser Version\n\nMicrosoft Edge Version 144.0.3719.82",
    "source": "issue",
    "source_url": "https://github.com/go-gitea/gitea/issues/36409",
    "source_id": 36409
  },
